The C++/WinRT package provides CMake targets:

    find_package(cppwinrt CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Microsoft::CppWinRT)

CPPWINRT_TOOL points to cppwinrt.exe.

When installed with the "modules" feature, CPPWINRT_MODULE_DIR is the module source directory and CPPWINRT_MODULE_FILES lists the generated module interface files (.ixx).

The modules require MSVC v14.50 (v145) or later and import the C++ standard library module. With CMake 4.4, enable its experimental import std support before project():

    set(CMAKE_EXPERIMENTAL_CXX_IMPORT_STD "f35a9ac6-8463-4d38-8eec-5d6008153e7d")

The required value changes between CMake releases. Then add the modules to a C++23 target:

    target_compile_features(main PRIVATE cxx_std_23)
    set_property(TARGET main PROPERTY CXX_MODULE_STD ON)
    target_sources(main
        PRIVATE
            FILE_SET cxx_modules TYPE CXX_MODULES
            BASE_DIRS ${CPPWINRT_MODULE_DIR}
            FILES ${CPPWINRT_MODULE_FILES}
    )
